 "about": "Front ES1: the es-419 glossary (plan analysis/front-plans/front-i18n-es.md §5.1) that src/i18n/es/es.test.ts enforces on every Spanish string. A term applies when its English pattern (case-insensitive regular expression) matches the English source: the Spanish must then contain the required stem. Names are fixed interface names: when the English contains one, the Spanish contains its Spanish form exactly. Forbidden words (matched with Unicode word boundaries) and patterns never appear in Spanish: Spain-only words, usted and its imperatives, voseo, and any claim that a translation is CLEA's. Kept names stay exactly as in English. The lint applies to the Spanish strings that exist, so rows for areas still in English wait for their sub-front. Style: tú, buttons and menu items in the infinitive, no voseo or Spain-only forms, paired ¿ ¡, the decimal point, a space before units, and the glyphs › … ↗ ▸ · kept. Translations are web adaptations by OpenVireo, never CLEA's.",
